SUMMARY:Cultural Immersion Saturday: China
DESCRIPTION:Each Saturday in May highlights a unique AANHPI culture\, with community partners taking the lead on experiences\, performances\, and vendors to showcase their heritage. \n\n\n\nJoin us Saturday\, May 23\, as Oregon Chinese Coalition brings us a full day honoring and celebrating Chinese culture. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTimeProgramDetails10:00 AM to 6:00 PMFood & Retail VendorsBeijing Bro\, Little Beijing\, Seremony Pavilion\, & Brandzy Studio10:30 AM – 1:30 PMCulture CornerAncient Currency Rubbing Workshop11:00 AMCultural Performance● Mulan Drum Team● Salem New Moon Dance  Troupe● WE Youth String Ensemble● Bluebell Dance Team11:00 AM – 12:00 PMCulture CornerTea Ceremony Demonstration11:00 AM – 12:30 PMCulture CornerCalligraphy Demonstration By the Artist12:30 PM – 1:30 PMCulture CornerCalligraphy Experience12:30 PM – 2:00 PMCulture CornerTaste of Home\, Where the Heart Belongs — Chinese Homestyle Cooking Demonstration1:00 PMCultural Performance● Salem New Moon Dance Troupe● Erin Qiu Violin Solo● Portland Harmonics● Yanmei Wang Beijing Opera● Salem New Moon Dance Troupe1:00 PM – 4:00 PMCulture CornerChinese YoYo Demo1:30 PM – 3:00 PMCulture CornerYang Qin Demo1:30 PM – 3:30 PMCulture CornerCalligraphy Demonstration By the Artist1:30 PM – 4:00 PMCulture CornerHanfu Showcase2:00 PM – 4:30 PMCulture CornerRubik’s Cube Activity3:00 PMCultural Performance● OCC Singing Group● Good Time Chinese School Dance Team● Seline Dai● Phoenix HanFu Society HanFu Show● Soda Dance Academy● OCC Dragonfly Diabolo Team\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMeet the Community Partner:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Oregon Chinese Coalition is a local Chinese organization dedicated to building a connected and united Chinese community that embraces diverse socioeconomic backgrounds\, political beliefs\, and religious and cultural traditions.  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nParking & Directions\n\n\n\nFree Lan Su Parking\n\n\n\nThere is free first come\, first served parking in our sister lot next to the garden at 424 NW Third Avenue. Additional metered parking and garages are available on surrounding streets.
URL:https://lansugarden.org/event/cultural-immersion-saturday-china/
LOCATION:Lan Su Chinese Garden\, 239 NW Everett Street\, Portland\, Oregon\, 97209
CATEGORIES:AANHPI Heritage Month,Free with admission or membership
