SUMMARY:Ancient Currency Rubbing Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Did you know China was the first civilization in the world to use paper currency? As early as the Song Dynasty\, paper money was already in circulation more than 600 years before it appeared in the West. \n\n\n\nIn this hands on workshop\, visitors will explore the history of ancient Chinese currency and discover how money evolved throughout different dynasties. Guests will also have the opportunity to create their own traditional Chinese paper money rubbing to take home as a unique cultural keepsake. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMeet the Community Partner:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Oregon Chinese Coalition is a local Chinese organization dedicated to building a connected and united Chinese community that embraces diverse socioeconomic backgrounds\, political beliefs\, and religious and cultural traditions.  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nParking & Directions\n\n\n\nFree Lan Su Parking\n\n\n\nThere is free first come\, first served parking in our sister lot next to the garden at 424 NW Third Avenue. Additional metered parking and garages are available on surrounding streets.
URL:https://lansugarden.org/event/ancient-currency-rubbing-workshop/
LOCATION:Lan Su Chinese Garden\, 239 NW Everett Street\, Portland\, Oregon\, 97209
CATEGORIES:AANHPI Heritage Month,Family Fun,Free with admission or membership
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://lansugarden.org/wp-content/uploads/Picture11-1.webp
