SUMMARY:Chinese Song Sing Along
DESCRIPTION:Sing\, play\, and explore Chinese music with Alan in an enjoyable and accessible session on Sundays. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n3:00 – 4:00 AM | Sundays\, May 10 – September 27\, 2026 \n\n\n\nJoin Alan for an enjoyable and accessible Chinese music experience! If you love music and are eager to try something new\, you are warmly invited to learn a Chinese song\, a verse\, or even just a single line with Alan. You are also welcome to bring your own instrument and play. Music and singing are wonderful ways to explore culture and connect with others. \n\n\n\nThis event is open to all—no language background is required. \n\n\n\n\nGet Admission\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMeet the Instructor: \n\n\n\nAlan Liang is an accomplished musician skilled in vocal performance\, guitar\, keyboard\, and drums. He is a member of the Huayun Arts Alliance and the founder of the OCC Northwest Music Club. Alan has long been an active supporter of Chinese music and performing arts in the Portland community. He has participated in numerous Lunar New Year celebrations and cultural festivals\, making ongoing contributions to the promotion of Chinese music and culture. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nParking & Directions\n\n\n\nFree Lan Su Parking\n\n\n\nThere is free first come\, first served parking in our sister lot next to the garden at 424 NW Third Avenue. Additional metered parking and garages are available on surrounding streets.
URL:https://lansugarden.org/event/chinese-song-sing-along-2/2026-05-24/
LOCATION:Lan Su Chinese Garden\, 239 NW Everett Street\, Portland\, Oregon\, 97209
CATEGORIES:Free with admission or membership,Learning,Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://lansugarden.org/wp-content/uploads/Picture1-4.webp
END:VEVENT
